// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 21-standard-library-semantics
// facility: §2h [Str-Value-View] (D-0302, D-0225): a `str` binding as a variant's `StringView` payload; conf.str-binding-view-in-variant
// kind: positive
// expect: ok
// expect-stdout-hex: 747275652061207374722062696e64696e670a
//
// Where a variant's payload is a `StringView` once the expected type has
// fixed it, a `str` binding is `StringView::of(t)`, as a literal is
// `StringView::of(L)` there (D-0225). Rejected before D-0302.
import std;

fn main()
{
    str t = "a str binding";
    Option<StringView> o = Some(t);
    printf("%v %s\n", Option::is_some(&o), Option::unwrap(o));
}
